  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 1.17,
      "end": 7.17,
      "text": "...275 and 285, also on stereo VHF. This is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.17,
      "end": 24.81,
      "text": "Hi there, this is Tommy Vance. Welcome to the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.81,
      "end": 27.81,
      "text": "And tonight, we've got sessions by The Only Ones, their latest session.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.81,
      "end": 30.81,
      "text": "One from 1975 by Stretch, who are now defunct.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.81,
      "end": 36.81,
      "text": "Classic tracks by The Byrds, Little Feet, Barclay James Harvest, Steve Hillage, Jethro Tull and Uriah Heep.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.81,
      "end": 48.86,
      "text": "You can hear cuts, new ones from Bill Nelson's new band, also from The Secret and Firefall.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.86,
      "end": 50.36,
      "text": "plus the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.74,
      "end": 52.0,
      "text": "Three tracks of pure delight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 54.08,
      "text": "and the answer to last week's FNC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.52,
      "end": 57.0,
      "text": "Somebody out there is in for a £10 record token.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.5,
      "end": 67.26,
      "text": "But this Friday, to get the whole thing underway,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.64,
      "end": 69.08,
      "text": "here is Rory Gallagher.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.08,
      "end": 535.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.2,
      "end": 111.24,
      "text": "He was on earlier on the programme,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.66,
      "end": 113.52,
      "text": "right in front of this very microphone.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.7,
      "end": 116.58,
      "text": "And I promised him I wouldn't play it at the wrong speed.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.04,
      "end": 117.88,
      "text": "And I did.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 119.28,
      "end": 121.45,
      "text": "I'll be banished for Derry.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.47,
      "end": 126.67,
      "text": "8 Miles High, a really classic track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.0,
      "end": 710.69,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 710.69,
      "end": 712.89,
      "text": "that was asked for by Andrew Darby of Odd Acres,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 712.99,
      "end": 715.63,
      "text": "Hockham's Lane, Renhold in Bedfordshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 717.14,
      "end": 718.7,
      "text": "Prior to that, you heard Souped Up Ford,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 718.8,
      "end": 721.28,
      "text": "which comes from a 10-inch four-track maxi-single",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 721.28,
      "end": 723.26,
      "text": "to be played at 45 RPM.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 723.9,
      "end": 725.08,
      "text": "Sorry I didn't start it that way.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 725.16,
      "end": 726.88,
      "text": "It was a combination of the fact that, well,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 726.9,
      "end": 729.42,
      "text": "it looked like a bit of an LP and my stupidity.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 729.42,
      "end": 733.54,
      "text": "Souped up Ford is by, of course, Rory Gallagher, that ace Irish guitarist.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 742.17,
      "end": 744.33,
      "text": "And now, let's hear something from the only ones.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 744.33,
      "end": 1241.07,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1239.74,
      "end": 1242.77,
      "text": "There's one of the real talents in the United Kingdom.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1242.77,
      "end": 1245.97,
      "text": "That's Ron Argent on a track from his new solo album, which is called Moving Home.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1246.07,
      "end": 1249.53,
      "text": "It's just come out on MCA, and the track was called Smiling.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1249.91,
      "end": 1253.99,
      "text": "Before that, the first of four from the band called The Only Ones, a session by them tonight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1254.29,
      "end": 1257.45,
      "text": "The track that you heard from them was Miles From Nowhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1257.83,
      "end": 1260.99,
      "text": "Well, I'm a few miles from [redacted address], Liverpool 17,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1261.47,
      "end": 1262.63,
      "text": "but I don't think Michael Bell is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1262.93,
      "end": 1263.87,
      "text": "Mike, this is for you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1263.87,
      "end": 1794.62,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1799.62,
      "end": 1801.64,
      "text": "That's Stretch, and you can't judge a book.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1804.64,
      "end": 1806.78,
      "text": "It's just the first of four ace numbers",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1806.78,
      "end": 1808.5,
      "text": "that we're going to be playing from a session",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1808.5,
      "end": 1810.88,
      "text": "that was recorded Friday the 12th of December,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1811.02,
      "end": 1814.0,
      "text": "way back in 1975, when Stretch were then together.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1814.85,
      "end": 1815.85,
      "text": "Which they ain't now.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1818.18,
      "end": 1820.32,
      "text": "Drunk it out of the archives because we got a really nice letter",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1820.32,
      "end": 1822.72,
      "text": "from a gentleman by the name of Kevin Daines,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1822.72,
      "end": 1826.72,
      "text": "who lives at Salford Lodge, [redacted address], Malvern, in Worcestershire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1827.6,
      "end": 1828.42,
      "text": "Care if you've got taste?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1828.82,
      "end": 1839.02,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Long Distance Love, and that was by the band called Little Feet.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1839.44,
      "end": 1842.7,
      "text": "For Michael Bell, up there, somewhere in Liverpool.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1845.41,
      "end": 1847.25,
      "text": "Bill Nelson's got a new band together.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1847.79,
      "end": 1852.59,
      "text": "Beautiful piece of music by Barclay James Harvest.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1852.59,
      "end": 2155.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2160.0,
      "end": 2378.8,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2378.8,
      "end": 2381.54,
      "text": "Came out on the album October in 1976.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2382.02,
      "end": 2388.8,
      "text": "Rock and roll star, it was called, and it was played because Thomas Hill, [redacted address], Finderne in Derby, wrote in and said,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2388.8,
      "end": 2390.3,
      "text": "Oi, Tom, play it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2392.41,
      "end": 2394.21,
      "text": "Before that, you heard a track from an album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2394.21,
      "end": 2396.11,
      "text": "that's not coming out till February the 16th.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2396.19,
      "end": 2398.21,
      "text": "The LP is going to be called Sound on Sound.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2398.37,
      "end": 2400.93,
      "text": "It's the first LP by Bill Nelson's Red Noise.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2401.45,
      "end": 2403.07,
      "text": "The cut you heard was out of touch.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2406.66,
      "end": 2408.52,
      "text": "If there's anything you particularly would like to hear,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2408.66,
      "end": 2409.96,
      "text": "just write to me, let me know.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2409.96,
      "end": 2415.14,
      "text": "Tommy Vance, Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1, London, W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2415.92,
      "end": 2417.14,
      "text": "And we'll dig it out of the archives.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2417.24,
      "end": 2419.82,
      "text": "That includes sessions as well, BBC Radio 1 sessions.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2420.88,
      "end": 2422.44,
      "text": "For Led Zeppelin fans, let me tell you",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2422.44,
      "end": 2426.16,
      "text": "that the 1969 session done by them will be broadcast on this show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2426.16,
      "end": 2428.86,
      "text": "on Friday, the 2nd of February.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2429.18,
      "end": 2430.52,
      "text": "But now, the only ones.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2430.98,
      "end": 2433.98,
      "text": "Written by George Harrison.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2433.98,
      "end": 2910.71,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2910.71,
      "end": 2913.91,
      "text": "That was from the album L by Steve Hillich, It's All Too Much.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2914.68,
      "end": 2917.74,
      "text": "And it was requested by quite a number of people, including Chris Perry.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2918.56,
      "end": 2920.98,
      "text": "He lives at the Barton, I think it's Lawn Hitton,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2921.3,
      "end": 2922.92,
      "text": "in Launceston, down there in Cornwall.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2923.16,
      "end": 2924.66,
      "text": "Wanted me to play it for the Perry brothers,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2925.02,
      "end": 2927.78,
      "text": "and also for all his mates and all the Blundells as well,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2928.12,
      "end": 2928.98,
      "text": "whoever they may be.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2929.44,
      "end": 2932.82,
      "text": "I also played it for a couple of people who live near the RCA factory up there",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2932.82,
      "end": 2936.18,
      "text": "that makes the records in Washington, Tyne and Weir, Carroll and Terry.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2936.66,
      "end": 2940.42,
      "text": "Before that you heard Flaming Torch by The Only Ones, but now back to Stretch.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3142.45,
      "end": 3144.99,
      "text": "Great session by Stretch, recorded in 1975.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3145.39,
      "end": 3146.47,
      "text": "Shame they are no more.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3146.85,
      "end": 3148.05,
      "text": "Kirby's gone off to do his own thing.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3148.11,
      "end": 3150.87,
      "text": "In fact, we played a track from his solo album a couple of weeks ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3151.33,
      "end": 3153.43,
      "text": "And Elmer Gantry's mucking around doing things as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3153.75,
      "end": 3155.95,
      "text": "Really nice session. That was called Livin' on the Highway.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3156.39,
      "end": 3158.97,
      "text": "Here's a nifty new single by The Secret.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3370.21,
      "end": 3372.51,
      "text": "The more I hear that, the more I like it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3372.81,
      "end": 3374.17,
      "text": "They've got a really good album out as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3374.25,
      "end": 3377.37,
      "text": "A new band by the name of The Secret and a single called Night After Night.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3377.63,
      "end": 3379.97,
      "text": "It's two minutes to eleven on the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3382.11,
      "end": 3410.39,
      "text": "Had a couple of letters this week saying,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3410.51,
      "end": 3412.95,
      "text": "what is this bit of music you use on the Friday Night Connection?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3413.53,
      "end": 3414.39,
      "text": "Well, I'll jog your memory.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3414.75,
      "end": 3417.79,
      "text": "It's the Radio One theme by Van de Graaff Generator.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3436.69,
      "end": 3439.85,
      "text": "Time to put a smile on the face of a man by the name of Ian Dart",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3439.85,
      "end": 3442.39,
      "text": "of [redacted address], Chudley, Endeavour.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3442.97,
      "end": 3446.61,
      "text": "Ian Dart, you scored a double top because yours was the letter that came out of the bag",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3446.61,
      "end": 3450.03,
      "text": "with the correct answer to last week's Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3451.51,
      "end": 3455.63,
      "text": "I'd say about a 97% success rate this week.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3456.03,
      "end": 3457.99,
      "text": "Can't fox you up anywhere at all.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3460.38,
      "end": 3463.18,
      "text": "Tracks were The King Will Come by Wishbone Ash,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3463.74,
      "end": 3464.98,
      "text": "Killer Queen by Queen,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3465.38,
      "end": 3467.58,
      "text": "and Princess of the Streets by The Stranglers.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3469.82,
      "end": 3471.76,
      "text": "Answer? Royalty.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3486.52,
      "end": 3488.6,
      "text": "Now, Mr. Dart has fulfilled his part of the deal",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3488.6,
      "end": 3490.62,
      "text": "for getting the £10 record voucher.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3491.12,
      "end": 3492.5,
      "text": "He's put together three bits of music",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3492.5,
      "end": 3494.32,
      "text": "with a very strong connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3494.86,
      "end": 3496.22,
      "text": "See if you can get it together.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4409.84,
      "end": 4411.2,
      "text": "15 minutes, Mr Dart.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4416.56,
      "end": 4418.68,
      "text": "And that was the Friday Night Connection of Mr Dart.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4418.86,
      "end": 4420.98,
      "text": "[redacted address], Chudley, down there in Devon.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4421.08,
      "end": 4422.86,
      "text": "£10 record token coming your way.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4423.32,
      "end": 4423.76,
      "text": "Congratulations.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4427.39,
      "end": 4428.09,
      "text": "Think you know the answer?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4428.25,
      "end": 4429.53,
      "text": "Think you know the Friday Night Connection?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4429.53,
      "end": 4431.65,
      "text": "Send your answers to Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4432.07,
      "end": 4437.26,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1, London, W1A, or WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4437.26,
      "end": 4448.06,
      "text": "why don't you do it right now it's 11 16 and here's johnny guitar watson track that's really",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4924.04,
      "end": 4928.72,
      "text": "well put together it's on atlantic it's a new album called ilan it's by the band called firefall",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4928.72,
      "end": 4932.36,
      "text": "and the track you heard was called get you back before that the new single by johnny guitar",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4932.36,
      "end": 4936.86,
      "text": "watson and what a guy he is to watch producing records in the studio he is absolutely amazing",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4936.86,
      "end": 4942.26,
      "text": "so full of energy and talent his single is called gangster of love back to the beach now on our",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4942.26,
      "end": 4951.26,
      "text": "session by the only ones. Ian Anderson and Jethro Tull, which of course was Aqualung,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4951.26,
      "end": 5215.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5220.0,
      "end": 5395.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5400.0,
      "end": 5495.52,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5495.52,
      "end": 5501.8,
      "text": "came out in 71. Track was Logomotive Breath, and we played it because Dave Kenny, 17 Parkway",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5501.8,
      "end": 5509.27,
      "text": "North, Wheatley and Doncaster, wanted to hear it. Hope he did, Dave. Oh, Dave, no joy, I'm",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5509.27,
      "end": 5513.17,
      "text": "afraid, at the moment on the Madison Square Garden concert that Jethro did. What?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5513.25,
      "end": 5522.07,
      "text": "just last year but maybe in the future before that a very short track one minute and ten seconds",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5522.07,
      "end": 5530.29,
      "text": "sid barrett from the lp barrett came out in 1970 the real tortured genius and that was requested",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5530.29,
      "end": 5537.23,
      "text": "by stephen tretheway of number 23 edgeway whimslow in cheshire steve i heartily agree with you not",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5537.23,
      "end": 5541.49,
      "text": "enough sid barrett on the radio these days but i don't agree with you when you say people have",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5541.49,
      "end": 5543.31,
      "text": "forgotten him. I don't think they really have.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5548.57,
      "end": 5549.89,
      "text": "And prior to that, from here to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5549.89,
      "end": 5551.95,
      "text": "eternity, by The Only",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5551.95,
      "end": 5555.96,
      "text": "Ones. Now,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5556.06,
      "end": 5559.06,
      "text": "more from Stretch. Elvis Costello",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5760.0,
      "end": 5897.56,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5897.56,
      "end": 5899.6,
      "text": "and the attractions from the LP Armed Forces,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5899.72,
      "end": 5901.58,
      "text": "already number two in the LP charts. The track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5901.58,
      "end": 5903.4,
      "text": "is called Moods for Moderns. It was for Jenny",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5903.4,
      "end": 5905.62,
      "text": "and Chris down there in Brighton. Before that,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5905.72,
      "end": 5907.24,
      "text": "Stretch from 1975",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5907.24,
      "end": 5909.38,
      "text": "and Hold On. This is for Janet",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5909.38,
      "end": 5911.6,
      "text": "Ryber, [redacted address],",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5912.02,
      "end": 5913.34,
      "text": "London, NW11,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5913.78,
      "end": 5915.44,
      "text": "who likes to hear music in a sleepy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5915.44,
      "end": 5918.44,
      "text": "state. He brings it back.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5940.0,
      "end": 6290.76,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6290.76,
      "end": 6293.48,
      "text": "came out in 1969, a classic track.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6293.9,
      "end": 6296.2,
      "text": "It's a Beautiful Day and White Bird for Janet,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6296.74,
      "end": 6298.34,
      "text": "who's still in a sleepy state, I would imagine.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6298.84,
      "end": 6300.32,
      "text": "Here's the finale from The Only Ones.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6300.78,
      "end": 6306.18,
      "text": "Put together in the BBC Studios just last December,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6492.42,
      "end": 6494.28,
      "text": "that was The Only Ones in their final track tonight,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6494.4,
      "end": 6496.04,
      "text": "Nice Session, the track was called Prisoner.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6496.44,
      "end": 6499.2,
      "text": "Way back in 75, Stretch put this together, Miss Jones.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6688.96,
      "end": 6692.06,
      "text": "Stretch, as they sounded way back in 1975 in the BBC Studios,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6692.16,
      "end": 6693.46,
      "text": "that track was called Miss Jones.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6693.8,
      "end": 6696.44,
      "text": "And all those cuts are on the album Elastique.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6696.44,
      "end": 6699.2,
      "text": "a nice session that must have been to attend.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6699.32,
      "end": 6702.36,
      "text": "All right, now, look at yourselves.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6702.9,
      "end": 6707.7,
      "text": "And look at yourselves, especially for Alan Roy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6840.0,
      "end": 7073.22,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7073.22,
      "end": 7075.1,
      "text": "up there in Snowbound in Burness.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7076.78,
      "end": 7078.38,
      "text": "And that's it for the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7078.72,
      "end": 7080.14,
      "text": "Good music, disc jockey's rubbish.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7082.2,
      "end": 7084.6,
      "text": "Thanks to our sessions, tonight the only ones in stretch,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7084.78,
      "end": 7086.02,
      "text": "both produced by Tony Wilson,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7086.24,
      "end": 7088.8,
      "text": "as is the whole programme, excluding the mistakes.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7091.0,
      "end": 7092.88,
      "text": "Our studio engineer tonight was John. Thank you, John.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7098.1,
      "end": 7101.48,
      "text": "Now, wherever you are, keep warm and enjoy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7101.88,
      "end": 7103.28,
      "text": "I'll see you next Friday at the same time.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7103.4,
      "end": 7104.3,
      "text": "Till then, ta-ta.",
      "source": "TV"
    }
  ]
}